      "goal": "Trace the perspective reversals and temporal polarity in Steiner’s account of light and darkness.",
      "key": "Steiner treats Hegel’s thought-world and Schopenhauer’s will-world as partial views. His account of reincarnation transforms earlier limb-will into present head-thought and present will into future thought. Through Imagination, Inspiration and Intuition, he says thought is experienced as light. He explicitly distinguishes that experience from seeing a second physical world. The head is thought inwardly and light outwardly; the cosmos is light inwardly and thought when imagined from outside.",
