      "key": "Steiner challenges the separation of a material cosmos from a religious world of moral reward and punishment. His bridge treats present nature as the outcome of earlier spiritual beings’ thought and deeds, and present human will as a seed of future nature. Darkness inwardly becomes will, virtue and love. Pure thinking is also filled with will, a point he links to The Philosophy of Freedom. Perceiving sunrise, sky, plants and sound with one’s whole humanity should awaken gratitude toward the beings whose earlier activity surrounds us.",
