      "key": "Steiner assigns architecture to the soul's departure from embodiment, dress to its arrival, and sculpture to spirit expressed in the present human form. Painting moves beyond their three-dimensional space. It should generate experienced nearness and distance through colour: red/yellow approach, blue/purple recede. He says linear perspective was historically necessary and must still be understood, but colour perspective should again become an artistic power. This practical proposal rests on a spiritual account: seeing mineral and plant colour awakens a memory of the divine beings' ancient creative activity.",
      "context": "The coloured-sheet analogy explains the intended memory relation: familiar movements with white sheets recall earlier red/green sheets. Steiner then attributes cosmic imagination to the eye itself. The lecture continues through painting's two dimensions, music's line in time and poetry's spiritual directions: epic from above, drama from below, lyric on the human plane. Its aim is to turn anthroposophical concepts into living form and feeling, rather than leave them as abstract definitions. These dimensional and cosmic claims belong to his spiritual scheme.",
